# Append-only docs: a local merge or rebase keeps both sides' added lines instead of stopping on a conflict
# (2026-10-21 harness hardening; every parallel branch appends to these two files).
#
# Caveats of the built-in `union` driver:
# - it never shows a conflict, so when both sides edit the SAME existing line both versions are kept (a stale line
#   survives next to the new one) and identical lines added on both sides can appear twice. Review the merged hunk
#   (`git diff ORIG_HEAD -- DECISIONS.md CHANGELOG.md`) after a rebase.
# - it applies to local git (merge, rebase, cherry-pick) only; GitHub's own conflict check ignores it, so rebase
#   locally before opening or merging the PR.
#
# CURRENT_STATE.md is deliberately NOT here: it has sections edited in place (the "status" sections), which union
# would silently duplicate. Resolve its conflicts with .claude/skills/quoky-ship/scripts/resolve_changelog.py (tracked).
DECISIONS.md merge=union
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
